## Custom configuration
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.custom.configuration" -}}
{{ template "custom.custom.configuration.header" . }}

### Streams and go2rtc.yaml

`config` becomes `/config/go2rtc.yaml`. Without `persistence.config` the file
is mounted read-only from a ConfigMap, so the values file is the only source
of truth and edits in the web UI are not saved. With `persistence.config`
enabled, the file is copied to the volume only if it does not exist yet; after
that the web UI (and go2rtc itself) own it.

```yaml
config:
  streams:
    front_door: rtsp://user:password@192.168.1.30:554/stream1
  webrtc:
    listen: ":8555"
    candidates:
      - 192.168.1.20:8555
      - stun:8555
```

Keep camera passwords out of the values file by referencing env vars
(`rtsp://user:${CAMERA_PASSWORD}@...`, supported by go2rtc) and loading them
from a Secret with `controllers.main.containers.main.envFrom`.

### Networking

WebRTC needs a UDP/TCP address that clients can reach on port 8555, and
HomeKit and some cameras rely on multicast. Two ways to get that:

- `defaultPodOptions.hostNetwork: true` (and `dnsPolicy: ClusterFirstWithHostNet`),
  the setup the go2rtc docs recommend.
- A `LoadBalancer` Service (`service.main.type: LoadBalancer`) with that IP in
  `config.webrtc.candidates`.

### Hardware transcoding

Use the `<version>-hardware` image tag (amd64) and mount the GPU, e.g.
`/dev/dri` through a `hostPath` persistence item, or use a device plugin.
{{- end -}}
